.TH TELEGRAM-NOTIFIER.TOML 5 "2026-09-15" "telegram-notifier 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
telegram\-notifier.toml \- configuration file for telegram\-notifierd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I /etc/telegram\-notifier/config.toml
configures
.BR telegram\-notifierd (8).
It is TOML. Unknown keys are an error rather than being ignored, so a typo is
caught by
.B telegram\-notifierd \-\-check
instead of silently doing nothing.
.PP
The file is installed as a dpkg conffile, so local edits survive upgrades. It
is owned
.B root:telegram\-notifier
mode
.BR 0640 ,
because it may contain the bot token.
.SH "SECTION [service]"
.TP
.B socket_path
Path of the control socket. Default
.IR /run/telegram\-notifier/notifier.sock .
.TP
.B socket_group
Group given ownership of the socket; its members may send notifications.
Default
.BR telegram\-notify .
If the group does not exist the daemon logs a warning and keeps its own
primary group, which effectively locks other users out. If the group exists
but cannot be assigned, startup fails rather than leaving a socket nobody can
reach. Set it to the empty string to skip the change entirely, which is
mainly useful when running the daemon as yourself, outside systemd.
.TP
.B socket_mode
Socket permissions as an octal string. Default
.BR "\(dq0660\(dq" .
.TP
.B state_dir
Directory holding the
.I queue
and
.I failed
subdirectories. Default
.IR /var/lib/telegram\-notifier .
.TP
.B log_level
One of
.BR error ", " warn ", " info ", " debug ", " trace .
Default
.BR info .
.TP
.B max_queue_size
Reject new messages once this many are pending, so a runaway sender cannot
fill the disk.
.B 0
disables the limit. Default
.BR 10000 .
.TP
.B min_send_interval_ms
Minimum delay between two Bot API calls. Default
.BR 50 ,
which stays below Telegram's overall limit of about 30 messages per second.
.SH "SECTION [telegram]"
.TP
.B bot_token
Token from @BotFather, inline. Mutually redundant with
.BR bot_token_file .
.TP
.B bot_token_file
File holding the token on a single line. Preferred: it keeps the secret in
its own file with its own permissions. Default installation uses
.IR /etc/telegram\-notifier/bot\-token .
.TP
.B api_base_url
Bot API endpoint. Default
.BR "\(dqhttps://api.telegram.org\(dq" .
Point this at a local Bot API server if you run one.
.TP
.B timeout_seconds
HTTP timeout per request. Default
.BR 15 .
.PP
The
.B TELEGRAM_NOTIFIER_BOT_TOKEN
environment variable, if set and non-empty, overrides both token settings.
This lets
.BR systemd.exec (5)
credentials supply the secret without it ever being written to disk.
.SH "SECTION [retry]"
.TP
.B max_attempts
Attempts before a message is moved to the
.I failed
directory.
.B 0
means retry forever. Default
.BR 10 .
.TP
.B initial_backoff_seconds
Delay before the second attempt. Default
.BR 5 .
.TP
.B backoff_multiplier
Factor applied to the delay after each failure. Must be at least
.BR 1.0 .
Default
.BR 2.0 .
.TP
.B max_backoff_seconds
Ceiling for the delay. Default
.BR 900 .
.PP
A
.B 429
reply from Telegram overrides this schedule with the delay Telegram requests.
.SH "SECTION [defaults]"
Values inherited by every target that does not override them.
.TP
.B target
Name of the target used when a client does not ask for one. It must match an
existing
.B [targets.*]
section.
.TP
.B format
.BR plain ", " markdown ", " markdownv2 " or " html .
Default
.BR plain ,
which sends text verbatim and cannot be rejected for bad markup.
.TP
.B silent
Deliver without a notification sound. Default
.BR false .
.TP
.B disable_link_preview
Suppress Telegram's link previews. Default
.BR true .
.SH "SECTION [targets.NAME]"
One section per recipient. At least one target is required, and
.B [defaults] target
must name one of them.
.TP
.B chat_id
Required. Numeric chat id, or
.B @channelusername
for a public channel. Group ids are negative; supergroup ids start with
.BR \-100 .
To find it, send a message to the bot and read
.I result[].message.chat.id
from
.IR https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates .
Note that bots have privacy mode enabled by default and therefore do not see
ordinary group messages: in a group, either send
.RB \(dq /start@yourbot \(dq
or turn privacy off with
.B /setprivacy
in @BotFather, otherwise the update list stays empty. For a channel, make the
bot an administrator and read
.I result[].channel_post.chat.id
instead.
.TP
.B message_thread_id
Forum topic id, for supergroups with topics enabled.
.TP
.B prefix
String prepended to every message sent to this target, useful for tagging the
sending host or environment.
.TP
.BR bot_token ", " bot_token_file
Per-target token, for sending as a different bot.
.TP
.BR format ", " silent ", " disable_link_preview
Override the corresponding
.B [defaults]
value for this target only.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.RS
.EX
[service]
socket_group = "telegram\-notify"

[telegram]
bot_token_file = "/etc/telegram\-notifier/bot\-token"

[defaults]
target = "ops"
format = "plain"

[targets.ops]
chat_id = "\-1001234567890"
message_thread_id = 42
prefix = "[db01] "

[targets.personal]
chat_id = "123456789"
silent = true
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR telegram\-notifierd (8),
.BR telegram\-notify (1)
